<title>SWEDEN: NCC unit win 430 mln SKR Oslo bank order.</title>
<headline>NCC unit win 430 mln SKR Oslo bank order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction company NCC on Wednesday said its Norwegian subsidiary Eeg-Henriksen had won an order to build a bank office in Oslo for 430 million crowns.  </p>
<p>The project, which would house the headquarters of Christiania Bank og Kreditkassen, would be completed in autumn 1998.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
